"Moon Thegund is a moon of Kimnor, a planet in the same solar system as Artona I."
"Half of Thegund is magically stabilized as the Thegund Protected Zone, where Avowed are common."
"The other half is wild and high in chaos, and largely uninhabited."
"Chaos acts like weather on Thegund, and outbreak forecasts read like weather reports."
"Demons are culled there, and outbreaks have been increasing."
"Thegund's chaos index rose for months and hit a limit shortly before Alden's visits."
"Thegund runs an old, primitive, poorly repaired System that answers to 'Contract'."
"Its System speaks garbled English, lacks features and fails outright in a demon swarm."
"Replacing Thegund's System would cause more degradation while chaos remains."
"Teleports to Thegund are the older, magically violent kind, barred one rank below B."
"Travel there needs an Artona I passport."
"The Elepta Agricultural Community and Yipalck's research facility are in its wild half."
"Demon swarms there are black, bee-like dots that pass through metal."
"Alden made nightly trips to Thegund to evacuate Joe's lab staff, one person per trip."
"Thegund's sky is always a dull yellow overcast of dingy, low-hanging clouds."
"Its day lasts about a month, followed by a long, cold, starless night."
"Its terrain varies little; demon bugs leave the ground sandy and caving."
"Its Contract is Contract Thegund; the outbreak is a Thegund Class corrupted environment."
"Help against outbreaks comes by spaceship from the Mother, and ships are scarce out there."
"Residents are tested yearly for chaos potential; those with high potential may not live there."
"A former city lies some distance beyond the first zone cleared of chaos."
"The System estimated rescue would take 8 to 14 months to reach Elepta."
"Chaos turned native grasshoppers into demon bugs; the whole species has high chaos potential."
"Thegund has perpetual cloud cover, no wind and no very large bodies of water."
"Its inhabited cities are on the other half, whose people begged the Mother for a knight."
"The Grand Senate would not spare knights to post there and once offered free relocation instead."
"Knight Alis-art'h, the Quaternary, cleansed the outbreak by Triforming the land."
"Triforming hurls soil into the sky and slams it down, leaving flat, fertile, chaos-free ground."
"Each day's cleansing bit a clean semicircle out of the chaos, with ground-shaking whumfs."
"Alis's ground team lived in a travel dome with a transparent roof, backed by a ship in orbit."
"Thegund's Contract collapsed entirely in the outbreak, and a new one took months to build."
"Thegund is a low-population backwater whose System was half-broken since before Earth's contract."
"Chayklo, reached by ship, is Thegund's only sizable city."
"Thegund's Museum of the Empire shows antique weapons and magic tools on open, unguarded tables."
"Kibby stole a white auriad from the museum, leaving a fake in its place."
"Only two unbonded auriads existed on all of Thegund."
"Joe claims a heritage right to inhabit Thegund's Luklo region."
"Chayklo holds poetry festivals; ruins of an abandoned city house a few reclusive people."
